        &= \frac{\frac{1}{\Gamma_k}-\frac{1}{\Gamma_{k-1}} - \frac{1}{\Gamma_k}\left(\frac{\Gamma_k}{\Gamma_{k-1}}\right)^s + \frac{1}{\Gamma_{k-1}}\left(\frac{\Gamma_{k-1}}{\Gamma_k}\right)^s}{\frac{1}{\Gamma_k^{1-s}} + \frac{1}{\Gamma_{k-1}^{1-s}}}.
    \end{align}
    Here, noting from the relation of $\Gamma_k$ and $\Gamma_{k-1}$ in \eqref{eq:GammaRelation} that $\Gamma_k \leq \Gamma_{k-1}$ and recalling that $s \in [1/2,1]$, we can make two observations. First, we have $\Gamma_k^{2s-1} \leq \Gamma_{k-1}^{2s-1}$, and hence
    \begin{align}
