        - \frac{1}{\Gamma_k}\left(\frac{\Gamma_k}{\Gamma_{k-1}}\right)^s + \frac{1}{\Gamma_{k-1}}\left(\frac{\Gamma_{k-1}}{\Gamma_k}\right)^s \geq 0.
    \end{align} 
    Second, we have $\Gamma_{k-1}^{1-s}\le \Gamma_k^{1-s}$, and hence
    \begin{align}
        \frac{1}{\Gamma_k^{1-s}} + \frac{1}{\Gamma_{k-1}^{1-s}}\leq \frac{2}{\Gamma_{k-1}^{1-s}}.
    \end{align}
    Combining the above two observations and recalling that $s=(1+\nu)/(1+3\nu)$ and the relations concerning $\Gamma_k$ and $\Gamma_{k-1}$ in  \eqref{eq:GammaRelation}, we have that
